#15823
Atop the Landslide~
   As you stand atop the mound of boulders an amazing sight spreads out before
you.  Fifteen horse lancers of the Royal Snow Bear Company sit fifty paces up
the canyon.  Their white chargers snorting steam and the pennon flags of their
lances snapping in the wind.  Ahead of the riders stand a hundred pikemen
armored in frost rimed breastplates.  In front of the footmen, there is a
contingent of swift, lightly armored front riders.  A rearguard of six lancers
and twenty footmen follow behind, while several scouts patrol ahead and to both
sides.    
~
